{% doc %}
  Renders the price zone of a product card: the "Pris" label (standard layout
  only), the headline price with an optional "Fra " prefix, the crossed-out
  compare-at price, and the unit-price suffix.
  Pure markup — the caller resolves the unit-pricing rule and passes the result.

  @param {object} product - required. Shopify Product object; used only to decide the "Fra " prefix.
  @param {object} variant - required. The card's variant; its `unit_price` is the headline when `has_unit_price`.
  @param {number} price - required. The product's price in cents.
  @param {number} [original_price] - Compare-at price in cents. Shown struck through when higher than `price`.
  @param {boolean} [has_unit_price] - True when the variant carries native Shopify unit pricing.
  @param {string} [unit_suffix] - Reference unit shown after the headline, e.g. 'm' or '100 g'. Only used when `has_unit_price`.
  @param {boolean} [is_minimal] - True for the 'minimal' card layout (no "Pris" label, smaller type).

  @example
  {% render 'product-card-price', product: product, variant: variant, price: price, original_price: original_price, has_unit_price: has_unit_price, unit_suffix: unit_suffix, is_minimal: is_minimal %}
{% enddoc %}

<div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-0.5 mt-1">
  {%- unless is_minimal -%}
    <span class="type-sm type-muted leading-none">Pris</span>
  {%- endunless -%}
  <div class="flex items-baseline gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
    <span class="type-md type-bold text-primary leading-none">
      {%- assign show_fra = false -%}
      {%- if product.variants.size > 1 and product.price_varies -%}
        {%- assign show_fra = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if show_fra -%}Fra {% endif -%}
      {%- if has_unit_price -%}{{ variant.unit_price | money }}{%- else -%}{{ price | money }}{%- endif -%}
    </span>
    {%- unless has_unit_price -%}
      {%- if original_price > price -%}
        <span class="type-sm type-muted line-through leading-none">{{ original_price | money }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- if has_unit_price -%}
      <span class="type-xs type-muted">/ {{ unit_suffix }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- comment -%}
    Surface 12: unit price sub-line, collection-card context. Omitted
    entirely here — when has_unit_price is true it's already the
    headline above (would print the same value twice); when false
    there's no unit-price data to show.
  {%- endcomment -%}
</div>
